{"id":"v11","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":11,"of":15,"title":"Written, closed, known","titleHe":"בֵּינוֹנִי פָּעוּל","goal":"Read the פָּעוּל form — the state an action leaves a thing in.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Beside the two passive binyanim there is a much simpler form, and it is far commoner than either: פָּעוּל. It is built straight off a pa'al root, it behaves like an adjective, and it names the state something has been left in."},{"type":"table","caption":"The verb, and the state it leaves behind","head":["verb","state"],"rows":[["כָּתַב — wrote","כָּתוּב — written"],["פָּתַח — opened","פָּתוּחַ — open"],["סָגַר — closed","סָגוּר — closed, shut"],["יָדַע — knew","יָדוּעַ — known"],["שָׁבַר — broke","שָׁבוּר — broken"],["אָהַב — loved","אָהוּב — beloved"],["מָכַר — sold","מָכוּר — sold"]]},{"type":"text","body":"It agrees like any adjective — כְּתוּבָה, פְּתוּחִים, סְגוּרוֹת — and it sits after its noun in the same place an adjective would."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הַחֲנוּת סְגוּרָה.","en":"The shop is closed."},{"he":"הַחַלּוֹן פָּתוּחַ.","en":"The window is open."},{"he":"זֶה כָּתוּב בַּסֵּפֶר.","en":"It's written in the book."},{"he":"הַסִּפּוּר הַזֶּה יָדוּעַ.","en":"This story is well known."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"This is not the past tense, and the difference matters. הַחֲנוּת סְגוּרָה says the shop is shut now; הַחֲנוּת נִסְגְּרָה says somebody shut it. One is a state, the other an event."},{"type":"tip","body":"Some have drifted so far from their verb that nobody hears one behind them any more: עָשׂוּי מֵעֵץ, made of wood, is a sentence about a table rather than about anybody making it. At that point the dictionary stops calling it a verb form and simply lists it as an adjective."}],"vocab":[{"he":"כָּתוּב","en":"written","translit":"katuv"},{"he":"פָּתוּחַ","en":"open","translit":"patuach"},{"he":"סָגוּר","en":"closed","translit":"sagur"},{"he":"שָׁבוּר","en":"broken","translit":"shavur"},{"he":"יָדוּעַ","en":"known","translit":"yadua"},{"he":"אָהוּב","en":"beloved","translit":"ahuv"},{"he":"עָשׂוּי","en":"made of, likely to","translit":"asuy"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["regarding","written","engineer","brother"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כָּתוּב","translit":"katuv"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["needs to (f.)","open","then","cold"],"correct":1,"prompt":"פָּתוּחַ","translit":"patuach"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["soul, self, person","worker, labourer","bone","closed"],"correct":3,"prompt":"סָגוּר","translit":"sagur"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["most of","and he said","what's new, how's it going","broken"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שָׁבוּר","translit":"shavur"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["ordinary, used to","known","tea","Sabbath loaf"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יָדוּעַ","translit":"yadua"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["beloved","fifth","forever, ever","lamp"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אָהוּב","translit":"ahuv"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["mum","made of, likely to","green (f.)","market"],"correct":1,"prompt":"עָשׂוּי","translit":"asuy"},{"type":"choice","q":"The verb, and the state it leaves behind — sold?","options":["סָגוּר","מָכוּר","כָּתוּב","פָּתוּחַ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"זֶה כָּתוּב ___.","en":"It's written in the book.","options":["אָהוּב","בַּסֵּפֶר","עָשׂוּי","יָדוּעַ"],"correct":1,"full":"זֶה כָּתוּב בַּסֵּפֶר."},{"type":"read","he":"יָדוּעַ","translit":"yadua","en":"known"},{"type":"choice","q":"The verb, and the state it leaves behind — broke?","options":["שָׁבוּר","סָגוּר","כָּתוּב","פָּתוּחַ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “made of, likely to”?","options":["מַזָּל טוֹב","שִׁעוּר","שָׂם","עָשׂוּי"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כָּתוּב","written"],["פָּתוּחַ","open"],["סָגוּר","closed"],["שָׁבוּר","broken"],["יָדוּעַ","known"]]},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___ הַזֶּה יָדוּעַ.","en":"This story is well known.","options":["יָדוּעַ","הַסִּפּוּר","עָשׂוּי","כָּתוּב"],"correct":1,"full":"הַסִּפּוּר הַזֶּה יָדוּעַ."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["שָׁבוּר","אָהוּב","כָּתוּב","סָגוּר"],"correct":3,"say":"סָגוּר","he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “closed” in Hebrew","answer":"סָגוּר","hint":"sagur"}]}